  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "A planar removed side creates nothing",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "A planar removed side creates nothing, beyond the census. Glue a knot space H1 into another along one simple 3-edge cut (a line of H1 into a point of H2) and remove a line on H1's side, which opens the cut. Take 24 planar knot spaces beyond the census: plane cubic bipartite incidence graphs of 10, 12 and 14 points, grown from the cube by ladder moves or taken from the prisms over 10-, 12- and 14-cycles and the truncated octahedron, each read both ways, with Kasteleyn signs, on which the knot is checked to fail. Spliced into K4^(3), census 6, the Fano plane and census 58, every knot crossing the opened cut after every removal on the planar side is generated by eliminations (up to ties) from knots on one side: 1612 removals, 724 of them with six-pattern interfaces, 432,867 crossing knots, none new. Over all ordered pairs of census spaces, planar removed sides create nothing (560 removals) while the non-planar ones (the Fano plane, census 58) create 936 new knots at 100 of 208 removals. No four-pattern interface creates (1400 removals), and every creating removal has a six-pattern interface and a non-planar removed side.",
